  "result": "The milestone feature is in place across schema, migration, types, services, events, audit, and alerts. The full suite passes (626 tests, including 9 new ones in `tests/services/milestone-service.test.ts`), and the typecheck and lint are clean.\n\nCalls I made that the spec left open:\n- Names are stored trimmed.\n- Moving an issue to the milestone it is already in is a no-op: nothing is published and a closed milestone does not refuse it.\n- Moving an issue publishes `issue.updated` with `changedFields: [\"milestoneId\"]`.\n- Each moved issue gets its own `issue_milestone_changed` alert, so an assignee with several moved issues receives several.\n- The audit summaries for milestone events are generic, because the event payloads carry only ids.\n\nI did not build any UI or server actions for milestones; the spec covered the service layer only.",
